1 passed, 2 failed. That was a filtered run of `CartViewModelTest` only; the module's other unit tests weren't part of it.

Both failures are the same error, from the test-results XML:

> Module with the Main dispatcher had failed to initialize. For tests Dispatchers.setMain from kotlinx-coroutines-test module can be used

`addItem` and `removeItem` launch on `viewModelScope`, which runs on `Dispatchers.Main`. On the local JVM there's no Android main looper, so anything launched there throws unless the test swaps the Main dispatcher. The test that passes presumably never launches a coroutine.

The usual fix is a small JUnit rule:

```kotlin
class MainDispatcherRule(
    private val dispatcher: TestDispatcher = UnconfinedTestDispatcher(),
) : TestWatcher() {
    override fun starting(description: Description) = Dispatchers.setMain(dispatcher)
    override fun finished(description: Description) = Dispatchers.resetMain()
}
```

plus `@get:Rule val mainRule = MainDispatcherRule()` in `CartViewModelTest`. Want me to add it? If other ViewModel tests need the same thing, I'd put the rule in a shared `testutil` package.
